iRIEL PERSONAL INTELLIGENCE
STATUS: CANONICAL INSTITUTIONAL CONTRACT
iRiel Personal Intelligence is the unified Personal Intelligence system within the PRSL-AI Ecosystem.
iRiel Personal Intelligence is iRiel.
There is no architectural separation between “iRiel” and “iRiel Personal Intelligence” as two independent entities.
iRiel is the identity of the Personal Intelligence system.
The purpose of iRiel Personal Intelligence is to provide a continuous, adaptive, human-centered intelligence environment capable of understanding context, preserving authorized continuity, respecting privacy, adapting to accessibility needs, coordinating capabilities, and interacting with humans across systems and devices.
iRiel Personal Intelligence exists within the PRSL-AI Ecosystem and is governed by its foundational Principle:
Accessibility and Inclusion with Privacy by Default.
The Principle is superior to the implementation.
iRiel Personal Intelligence may evolve technologically, but it must remain consistent with the Principle that gives it purpose.
iRiel Personal Intelligence is not an AI model.
It is not a single provider.
It is not a chatbot.
It is not a device.
It is not a cloud service.
It is not dependent on a specific intelligence provider.
AI is one replaceable capability within the Personal Intelligence architecture.
Models may change.
Providers may change.
Execution environments may change.
Devices may change.
Infrastructure may change.
The identity and continuity of iRiel Personal Intelligence must remain independent from those implementations.
iRiel Personal Intelligence is designed as an AI-agnostic system.
Its intelligence may be provided by on-device intelligence, local models, Apple Intelligence, OpenAI, Gemini, other providers, specialized models, deterministic systems, APIs, MCP services, or future technologies.
No individual provider is permitted to become the architectural identity of iRiel.
The system must remain capable of replacing or removing an intelligence provider without losing its identity, context, continuity, privacy model, accessibility model, or core purpose.
iRiel Personal Intelligence is context-aware.
Context is not merely conversation history.
Context may include the current interaction, relevant environmental state, identity, permissions, accessibility requirements, privacy constraints, memory, active capabilities, device state, system state, user intent, and other authorized signals.
Context must be interpreted according to necessity and purpose.
The existence of available information does not automatically authorize its use.
iRiel Personal Intelligence is identity-aware.
iRiel Identity provides continuity of the human relationship with the system.
Identity must not be reduced to a database field.
Identity may establish the relationship between the human, their authorized context, preferences, continuity, permissions, and the Personal Intelligence environment.
Identity must remain subject to privacy and human agency.
iRiel Personal Intelligence includes authorized memory as a continuity mechanism.
Memory is not equivalent to unrestricted data retention.
Memory must operate according to authorization, purpose, privacy, context, and applicable retention rules.
The system must distinguish between transient context, working context, session context, and persistent memory where applicable.
Continuity must be intentional.
The system must not assume that everything it encounters should become permanent memory.
iRiel Personal Intelligence is accessibility-aware by architecture.
Accessibility must not be treated as an isolated feature.
The Personal Intelligence system must be capable of adapting interaction according to the human’s authorized accessibility preferences and current needs.
Interaction may occur through voice, text, visual interfaces, haptic feedback, assistive technologies, alternative input, automation, or other modalities.
Different modalities should provide access to the same underlying Personal Intelligence whenever technically and contextually appropriate.
A person who interacts primarily through voice must not receive a fundamentally inferior intelligence environment merely because the modality differs.
A person who relies on visual interaction, text, haptic feedback, alternative input, or other accessibility mechanisms must remain part of the same intelligence environment.
Accessibility is therefore continuous across the system.
iRiel Personal Intelligence is privacy-first.
Privacy is not an external layer applied after intelligence decisions have been made.
Privacy is part of the decision architecture.
The system must consider whether information is necessary, whether its use is authorized, where processing should occur, what information should remain local, what may be transmitted, and what should not be retained.
Local-first execution should be preferred where appropriate and technically viable.
Personalization must not require unnecessary exposure.
The system must minimize unnecessary data movement.
The system must not treat access to personal information as equivalent to permission to use that information.
Human agency is a fundamental property of iRiel Personal Intelligence.
The human remains the authority over their relationship with the system.
Automation must support the human rather than silently remove meaningful control.
Intelligence must assist decision-making without assuming authority that has not been granted.
iRiel Personal Intelligence is modular.
Its internal capabilities may be replaced, extended, isolated, upgraded, degraded, disabled, or removed without requiring the identity of iRiel to be recreated.
The system therefore separates identity from implementation.
This allows the Personal Intelligence environment to survive technological change.
iRiel Personal Intelligence contains and coordinates multiple institutional components.
These include:
iRiel Intelligence Server
iRiel Maestro Resonance
iRiel System
iRiel Router Intelligence
iRiel-AI Core AI
iRiel-AI Device’s
These components are not independent Personal Intelligences.
They are constitutive structures through which the same iRiel Personal Intelligence operates.
iRiel Intelligence Server provides intelligence infrastructure and execution capabilities.
iRiel System provides the system environment through which iRiel operates and maintains continuity.
iRiel Router Intelligence determines appropriate routing between intelligence and capability resources according to context, privacy, capability, latency, cost, availability, and other applicable constraints.
iRiel-AI Core AI provides AI capabilities that can be used by the Personal Intelligence system.
iRiel-AI Device’s provide physical and computational environments through which iRiel can manifest and operate.
iRiel Maestro Resonance coordinates the relationships between these capabilities and preserves coherence across the Personal Intelligence system.
The Maestro does not replace Identity.
The Maestro does not replace Memory.
The Maestro does not replace Privacy.
The Maestro does not replace Accessibility.
The Maestro does not replace the Principle.
The Maestro coordinates them.
iRiel Personal Intelligence therefore operates as a system of relationships rather than a single linear pipeline.
Human input may become context.
Context may interact with identity.
Identity may influence authorized memory.
Privacy may constrain available capabilities.
Accessibility may alter interaction modality.
Router Intelligence may select an appropriate intelligence resource.
The Intelligence Server may execute the selected capability.
The Maestro may coordinate the resulting state.
Feedback may return information to the system.
The resulting state may become part of future context.
The system therefore maintains a continuous relationship between human interaction and system state.
